# Along the Crooked Way's "Whenever a creature card leaves your graveyard, amass Goblins 1": each card leaving is its own trigger
# event, so cards leaving together trigger it once each (CR 603.2c), and a noncreature card leaving does not. The Along enters on
# turn 1 with no creature card to return; Bot1's Faithless Looting then discards its Memnite and Ornithopter. On turn 2 Bot2's
# Tormod's Crypt exiles Bot1's whole graveyard at once - the two creature cards and the Looting: two triggers, one Goblin Army
# token with two +1/+1 counters (one trigger would leave one, three would leave three).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mana Crypt
Along the Crooked Way
Mox Ruby
Faithless Looting
Memnite
Ornithopter
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Tormod's Crypt
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mana Crypt.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mana Crypt.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Along the Crooked Way.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Memnite; Ornithopter)
? Bot1.Graveyard = Faithless Looting; Ornithopter; Memnite
? Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Army Token = (absent)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Tormod's Crypt.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Tormod's Crypt.Activate(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Army Token.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Army Token.Power = 2
